<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- BIO-CRD-007 owns api/features/bio-crd-007/** only. No ProjectReference to
         Biolog.Api.csproj (one-way dependency, scripts/check-module-project-references.sh)
         and no ProjectReference to api/features/bio-crd-005 either, despite that being a real
         runtime dependency (gating activation on a passed production job still needs to read
         and finally activate a real BIO-CRD-005 card issue): every cross-feature runtime need
         in this codebase goes through a narrow gateway interface THIS project defines (see
         Domain/ICardIssueGateway.cs) implemented by an adapter in
         api/Biolog.Api/Modules/BioCrd007Module.cs, the same shape every prior story in this
         epic already established.

         "Dependencies: BIO-CRD-006, BIO-CRD-004" in the approved story is build-wave
         sequencing, not runtime coupling, matching this epic's established precedent - no AC
         here names report/recover/replace or a card-designer canvas object; BIO-CRD-004's own
         template/barcode/signature outputs are referenced only as opaque strings in this
         project's own ProductionJob, never resolved here, the same shape BIO-CRD-005's own
         CardIssueProvenance already established.

         Namespace root is "CardProduction". No new ADR-0001 canonical identifier type is
         minted - a production job is keyed by its own natural composite
         (TenantId, PersonId, CardClass, SequenceNumber, JobSequenceNumber), reusing BIO-CRD-005's
         own card-issue key plus a job-attempt number this project owns. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.CardProduction.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
